{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","title":"color","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/color"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/color","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/color":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/color","abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"title":"color","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/color","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"title":"MXLColor","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLEnding"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending","abstract":[{"text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLEnding","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","kind":"symbol"}}}